      \field{abstract}{Though enterprise resource planning ({ERP}) has gained some prominence in the information systems ({IS}) literature over the past few years and is a significant phenomenon in practice, through (a) historical analysis, (b) meta-analysis of representative {IS} literature, and (c) a survey of academic experts, we reveal dissenting views on the phenomenon. Given this diversity of perspectives, it is unlikely that at this stage a broadly agreed definition of {ERP} can be achieved. We thus seek to increase awareness of the issues and stimulate further discussion, with the ultimate aim being to: (1) aid communication amongst researchers and between researchers and practitioners; (2) inform development of teaching materials on {ERP} and related concepts in university curricula and in commercial education and training; and (3) aid communication amongst clients, consultants and vendors. Increased transparency of the {ERP}-concept within {IS} may also benefit other aligned fields of knowledge.}
